From d23ae015137574b373352ff0ab3ffa56680401e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:57:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin I-447: per-doodad grass bend - each ground-effect
 doodad's root and tip measured from its own model (Living Azeroth's scan), so
 atlas-card grass sways and flat decals stay still

- HD::GrassBendCodes: root V = mean V of the lowest 12% of the height, tip V of the highest 12%; bend = saturate((t-0.3)/0.7)^2
  with t = (v - rootV)/(tipV - rootV); under 0.15 yd = flat, never moves; GroundEffectDoodadWind.cdbc (37 Seyris rows) overrides
- the bend rides as a 7-bit code in the vertex colour alpha beside the baked shadow (lit = 255 - code), written only while
  our grass shaders are in place; grass buffers refill when that flips; the HdGrass vertex shader decodes it (new key be0092c6)
- hdGrassBendShow <id> / hdGrassBendInfo for checking a doodad's measurement

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UHcJJVC4feQ4s15e9bNRoN
